{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: none.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The program does not score any top-level data variable with a sampling statement; `M`, `N`, `x0`, and `X` are context inputs. Each parameter (`alpha`, `beta`, and `inv_phi`) has exactly one built-in prior sampling statement before any model-block use, and the program does not use forbidden arbitrary log-density manipulation.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> M; // Number of covariates
  int<lower=0> N; // Number of observations

  vector[M] x0;   // Covariate baselines
  matrix[N, M] X; // Covariate design matrix
}

transformed data {
  matrix[N, M] deltaX;
  for (n in 1:N) {
    deltaX[n,] = X[n] - x0';
  }
}

parameters {
  real alpha;            // Intercept
  vector[M] beta;        // Slopes
  real<lower=0> inv_phi; // Dispersion parameter
}

model {
  // Prior model
  alpha ~ normal(3, 0.2);
  beta ~ normal(0, log(1.28));
  inv_phi ~ normal(0, 1); // Expand around initial Poisson mode
}

// Simulate a full observation from the current value of the parameters
generated quantities {
  vector[N] mu = exp(alpha + deltaX * beta);
  array[N] int y_pred = neg_binomial_2_log_rng(alpha + deltaX * beta, inv(inv_phi));
}

